S140 LRC14 C27 -> q=3 UNITAL BLOCK-LIFT AUDIT
==============================================================================
[0] Assumption challenge / quotient declaration
  considered vertices:
    C27 residues, antipodal shells, hole/double statuses, AP/GW labels,
    q=3 unital points, unital 4-blocks, branch-local charts, and
    S138 two-hole proof obligations.
  chosen test predicate:
    whether a marked transfer packet can be a q=3 unital 4-block
    without violating lambda=1 pair uniqueness.
  quotient preserves:
    C27 hole/double shell pair, branch label, and unital pair incidence.
  quotient destroys:
    exact time geometry, within-shell orientation beyond the antipodal
    pair, and any global ordering of unital points.
  challenged assumption:
    all marked transfers can live in one unital chart.  The test shows
    branch-local charts work, but the GW/K33 superposition repeats a pair.

[1] q=3 unital design sanity
  points=28 blocks=63 block_size_hist={4: 63}
  projective-line intersection sizes={1: 28, 4: 63}
  block intersection histogram={0: 945, 1: 1008}
  readout: two distinct unital blocks never share two points.

[2] C27 transfer packets as residue-pair 4-blocks
  GW  GW H12->D3         branch=tight-floor          block=(3, 12, 15, 24)
  K33 K33 H12->D9        branch=K33-unit-excess      block=(9, 12, 15, 18)
  P10 petal H10->D7      branch=C27-petal-two-block  block=(7, 10, 17, 20)
  P13 petal H13->D1      branch=C27-petal-two-block  block=(1, 13, 14, 26)

  simultaneous low-frontier repeated pairs={(12, 15): 2}
  obstruction:
    GW and K33 both contain the hole pair (12,15).  Since a q=3
    unital has lambda=1, those two packets cannot both be blocks in
    one unital chart under the raw residue-pair lift.

[3] Global AP/GW-label block model
  GW  block=('AP', 'D3', 'GW', 'H12')
  K33 block=('AP', 'D9', 'GW', 'H12')
  P10 block=('AP', 'D7', 'GW', 'H10')
  P13 block=('AP', 'D1', 'GW', 'H13')
  repeated pairs={('AP', 'GW'): 4, ('AP', 'H12'): 2, ('GW', 'H12'): 2}
  readout:
    treating AP and GW as two global points in every transfer block is
    worse: the pair (AP,GW) repeats immediately.  AP/GW labels must be
    chart labels or branch colors, not universal block vertices.

[4] Branch-local q=3 unital chart test
  tight chart: GW + both petals                 status=EMBEDS
    desired_blocks=[(3, 12, 15, 24), (7, 10, 17, 20), (1, 13, 14, 26)]
    example_unital_block_indices=[0, 1, 2]
    example_unital_blocks=[(20, 21, 26, 27), (4, 5, 6, 7), (9, 12, 19, 24)]
  K33 chart: near-miss + both petals            status=EMBEDS
    desired_blocks=[(9, 12, 15, 18), (7, 10, 17, 20), (1, 13, 14, 26)]
    example_unital_block_indices=[0, 1, 2]
    example_unital_blocks=[(20, 21, 26, 27), (4, 5, 6, 7), (9, 12, 19, 24)]
  global low frontier: GW + K33 + petals        status=FAIL(pair-repeat)
    desired_blocks=[(3, 12, 15, 24), (9, 12, 15, 18), (7, 10, 17, 20), (1, 13, 14, 26)]
    repeated_pairs={(12, 15): 2}
  S138 splice drop(10,12)->add(20,24)           status=EMBEDS
    desired_blocks=[(7, 10, 17, 20), (3, 12, 15, 24)]
    example_unital_block_indices=[0, 1]
    example_unital_blocks=[(20, 21, 26, 27), (4, 5, 6, 7)]
  S138 splice drop(10,12)->add(20,36)           status=EMBEDS
    desired_blocks=[(7, 10, 17, 20), (9, 12, 15, 18)]
    example_unital_block_indices=[0, 1]
    example_unital_blocks=[(20, 21, 26, 27), (4, 5, 6, 7)]
  12-branch superposition only                  status=FAIL(pair-repeat)
    desired_blocks=[(3, 12, 15, 24), (9, 12, 15, 18)]
    repeated_pairs={(12, 15): 2}

  splice readout:
    The two S138 genuine two-hole rows are not new single unital blocks.
    Each is a two-block path: petal H10->D7 plus either the GW block
    H12->D3 or the K33 near-miss block H12->D9.

[5] Tournament Analysis on lift obligations
  vertices: lift obligations/proof carriers, not runners.
  pair observable, ordered lexicographically:
    theorem-scale retention, C27 predicate retention, lambda=1 incidence,
    finite checkability, anti-scalar guard.
  fingerprint: score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1, 6: 1} c3=0 hp=1
  Hamiltonian path:
    exact M/Farey branch > C27 marked transfer > unital pair-repeat obstruction > branch-local q3 unital chart > S138 two-block splice path > global AP/GW vertex model > raw unital analogy

[6] Verdict
  Negative global result:
    the raw C27 residue-pair lift cannot put GW H12->D3 and K33
    H12->D9 into the same q=3 unital, because the hole pair (12,15)
    would occur in two different blocks.
  Positive local result:
    each branch separately embeds into the q=3 unital incidence design,
    and the S138 genuine two-hole rows lift as two-block splices.
  Proof-use refinement:
    use the unital as a branch-local pair-unique chart or splice grammar,
    not as a universal atlas for all C27 marked transfers at once.
